=== HANDLER_DIFF ===
--- internal/api/fleet_telemetry_handler.go (NEW, 224 lines) ---
+ FleetTelemetryHandler{cfg *config.Config}
+ NewFleetTelemetryHandler(cfg *config.Config) *FleetTelemetryHandler
+ CurrentSubscription(w, r) — GET /api/v1/tesla/fleet-telemetry/subscription
    body, _ := teslaconfig.NewBuilder() (host/port overridden from cfg.FleetTelemetry).BuildSubscription()
    w.Write(body) with application/json content-type.
    NO DB access. Replaces legacy SELECT FROM fleet_telemetry_subscriptions.
+ Coverage(w, r) — GET /api/v1/tesla/fleet-telemetry/coverage
    routes := router.LoadMap()
    For each (field, entry) in routes:
      - lookup category via protomodel.SignalsByName[field], or via
        compound-parent prefix match (algorithm shared with
        internal/tesla/router/coverage_test.go) for flattened children
        like LocationLatitude / TpmsHardWarningsFrontLeft.
      - lookup subscribed flag via teslaconfig.NewBuilder().SubscriptionFields()
        with the same flattened-child -> compound-parent fallback.
      - dual-writes (also_signal_log:true) increment signal_log totals
        too, matching runtime fan-out semantics.
    Response: { categories: [...], destination_totals: {...}, orphan_fields: [...] }
    Sorted deterministically (categories alphabetic, fields per category
    alphabetic, orphans alphabetic) so byte-stable across requests.

--- internal/api/fleet_telemetry_error_handler.go (UPDATED) ---
@@ imports
+ "github.com/prometheus/client_golang/prometheus"
+ _ "github.com/ev-dev-labs/teslasync/internal/tesla/normalize"
    Side-effect import registers tesla_normalize_unit_context_missing_total
    against prometheus.DefaultRegisterer at api package init time so
    MissingUnitDrops returns a real (zero-valued) family even on
